+   "body": "<<passages (unscreened): HB-26 §1, HB-26 §2, HB-26 §3>>\n--- HB-26 §1 | Memo: bike-leasing allowance exceptions — Purpose | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-03-01\nThis memo lists group exceptions to the bike-leasing allowance in HB-32. The facilities publishes worked examples of the bike-leasing allowance on the intranet. Each claim for the bike-leasing allowance needs a receipt showing the date, the amount and the supplier.\n--- HB-26 §2 | Memo: bike-leasing allowance exceptions — Exception for cargo bikes | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-03-01\nFor cargo bikes, the bike-leasing allowance is 80 EUR per month instead of the standard amount. Questions about the bike-leasing allowance go to the facilities, who keeps the record of decisions. Managers confirm claims for the bike-leasing allowance before payment in the next payroll run.\n--- HB-26 §3 | Memo: bike-leasing allowance exceptions — Carve-out | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-03-01\nThe exception above does not apply to cargo bikes used for private deliveries; they follow the standard bike-leasing allowance in HB-32 §2. The facilities reviews the bike-leasing allowance once a year and announces changes in advance. Claims for the bike-leasing allowance are filed in the expense tool under 'Benefits policy: bike leasing'.\n<<end passages>>\n"
